Title: Let ANGLE fall back to an older d3dcompiler it has to load itself
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

ANGLE's D3D9 backend compiles its HLSL through d3dcompiler, and on Windows XP it
never gets one. The copy shipped alongside Electron is d3dcompiler_47.dll from
the Windows SDK, a prebuilt binary that statically imports FlsAlloc, FlsFree,
FlsGetValue, FlsSetValue and InitializeCriticalSectionEx from kernel32 -- all
Vista additions -- so XP's loader rejects it outright. It is not ours to relink,
so winwrap cannot reach it the way it reaches everything else we build. On Vista
it loads fine; this is XP only.

HLSLCompiler already knows about older versions, but not in a way that helps.
Its list of names is swept with GetModuleHandleExA, which only adopts a compiler
some other module in the process has already loaded, and the LoadLibrary that
follows asks for the single version ANGLE was built against. Nothing tries to
load an older compiler that is present but not yet in the process -- which is
the only kind XP can offer.

So after both existing attempts fail, try LoadLibrary on each name in the list.
That reaches d3dcompiler_43.dll from the June 2010 DirectX redistributable,
which XP can load and which exports the D3DCompile that ensureInitialized
requires. Ordering is unchanged, so a machine with a current compiler still gets
it and this never runs.

Only D3DCompile is actually required -- the D3DDisassemble fetched next is behind
an ASSERT, so it is debug-only -- and every version in the list exports both.

diff --git a/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/d3d/HLSLCompiler.cpp b/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/d3d/HLSLCompiler.cpp
index 479e8b7..45770bc 100644
--- a/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/d3d/HLSLCompiler.cpp
+++ b/third_party/angle/src/libANGLE/renderer/d3d/HLSLCompiler.cpp
@@ -148,6 +148,36 @@ angle::Result HLSLCompiler::ensureInitialized(d3d::Context *context)
         }
     }
 
+#    if defined(ANGLE_PRELOADED_D3DCOMPILER_MODULE_NAMES)
+    if (!mD3DCompilerModule)
+    {
+        // The sweep above only adopts a compiler another module in this process already
+        // loaded; the load just attempted is of one version, the one this was built
+        // against. Neither finds an older compiler that is installed but not yet loaded,
+        // which is the only kind Windows XP has: d3dcompiler_47.dll imports FlsAlloc and
+        // InitializeCriticalSectionEx from kernel32, so it cannot load there at all and
+        // the D3D9 renderer dies before compiling its first shader. d3dcompiler_43.dll,
+        // from the June 2010 DirectX redistributable, has no such imports and supplies
+        // the shader models the D3D9 backend asks for.
+        //
+        // Only D3DCompile is actually required of it -- the D3DDisassemble below is
+        // behind an ASSERT -- and every version in this list exports both.
+        for (size_t i = 0; i < ArraySize(d3dCompilerNames); ++i)
+        {
+            mD3DCompilerModule = LoadLibraryA(ANGLE_UNSAFE_TODO(d3dCompilerNames[i]));
+            if (mD3DCompilerModule)
+            {
+                WARN() << "Loaded fallback D3D compiler "
+                       << ANGLE_UNSAFE_TODO(d3dCompilerNames[i]) << ".";
+                ANGLE_HISTOGRAM_ENUMERATION("GPU.ANGLE.D3DCompilerLoadLibraryResult",
+                                            D3DCompilerDefaultLibrarySuccess,
+                                            D3DCompilerEnumBoundary);
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+#    endif  // ANGLE_PRELOADED_D3DCOMPILER_MODULE_NAMES
+
     if (!mD3DCompilerModule)
     {
         DWORD lastError = GetLastError();
